0..76 Comment "// A recursive call at a variable converts through the arm that waits on it."
77..145 Comment "// `windWords(Loop(x))` runs to the `Loop` arm, whose `run` waits on"
146..225 Comment "// `windWords(x)`, stuck at the variable; an endpoint\'s computation is pure, so"
226..288 Comment "// the bind reads as the arm\'s constructor over the held call,"
289..367 Comment "// `S(windWords(x))`, and the kernel replays the reading by forcing it. An arm"
368..444 Comment "// that cases on the call before it returns keeps the call stuck, and a path"
445..521 Comment "// stating a value for it is refused. Conversion is definitional equality by"
522..600 Comment "// computation (Martin-Löf, _Intuitionistic Type Theory_, Bibliopolis, 1984)."
602..650 Comment "// The presented integers and the free naturals."
